Falsifies `memory_region_heap::verification::a_grow_never_commits_past_the_maximum`.

The defect: the plan caps the growth at the whole cap instead of at the room left under it, so a
heap that already holds pages is allowed to map as many again as the cap holds. The doubling term
and the request both reach it, and the committed range then leaves the cap.

Expected to fail: the harness's arithmetic on the committed range after a run of `got` pages
(an addition overflow, and the bound `after <= maximum`). Red in under a second on 2026-11-15.

diff --git a/crates/memory_region_heap/src/lib.rs b/crates/memory_region_heap/src/lib.rs
index b961c1948..bfbbaa69f 100644
--- a/crates/memory_region_heap/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/memory_region_heap/src/lib.rs
@@ -473,7 +473,7 @@ fn growth_pages(committed: u64, maximum: u64, need: u64) -> Option<(u64, u64)> {
     let want_pages = need_pages
         .max(committed / PAGE_BYTES) // doubling: as many again as we have
         .max(MINIMUM_GROW_PAGES)
-        .min(maximum.saturating_sub(committed) / PAGE_BYTES);
+        .min(maximum / PAGE_BYTES);
     if want_pages < need_pages {
         return None;
     }
